    <item>
      <title>Minute Maid is discontinuing its frozen juices. For this writer, there's no love lost</title>
      <link>https://www.phillyvoice.com/minute-maid-frozen-orange-juice/?utm_source=pv-rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=pv-site</link>
      <description>Minute Maid is retiring its frozen juices, which date to 1946. The news left some feeling nostalgic, but this writer is shedding no tears. Mixing the frozen concentrate was a tiresome task while she was growing up, and the orange juice also played a role in a traumatic childhood experience.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.phillyvoice.com/minute-maid-frozen-orange-juice/?utm_source=pv-rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=pv-site</guid>
